    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0128" n="8" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg8"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Sorsby to the Acting Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">La Paz,
                                Bolivia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 185.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm the receipt of
                    your sad message of the 1st instant, and to say that I immediately notified the
                    government, which as an expression of sympathy displayed the government flag at
                    half-mast on all government buildings, and that the flag of this legation was
                    displayed at half-mast on the 2d, 3d, and 4th, as a symbol of mourning.</p>
                <p>The expression of condolence by the government and officials by the foreign
                    representatives, as well as others of prominence here, has been general and
                    genuine, and, personally, I have the honor to request that my most profound
                    sympathy in this great loss to the country be conveyed to the President.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William B.
                    Sorsby.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
